# Panelize (this app)

Before writing or changing UI, read `node_modules/panelize/llms.txt` and `node_modules/panelize/docs/composition.md`.

- Import from `'panelize'`. Wrap the tree with `PanelizeProvider`.
- `Panels` is the view shell. Direct children are only `Panel` (one is allowed).
- `Row` only under `Rows` (two or more). `Col` only under `Cols` (two or more). `Cell` only under `Grid` (two or more).
- One band of content → `Panel` or `Div`, not a track of one item.
- The wrapper owns place (`alignX` / `alignY`, `flex`, `fill`, `gap`). Controls do not position themselves.
- Visible copy uses `Text` / `Heading` / `Span` / `TextLink` / `Label`.
- Custom components use `usePanelizeTheme` (or inherit `--panelize-*` from the nearest `Panel`). Do not invent a parallel palette.
- Forms, buttons, and chips are bonus. Core is panels, tracks, grid, and text.
